{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And HaShem your Elohim will circumcise, etc.</b> There is a fine point to examine: after it said above ״וְשַׁבְתָּ עַד ה׳ וְשָׁמַעְתָּ בְּקוֹלוֹ״, what place is there to say further ״וּמָל ה׳״? Further, I see that it says yet afterward ״וְאַתָּה תָשׁוּב״ etc., which appears to indicate that what preceded had not yet reached repentance — but this is not so, for after His circumcising his heart to love HaShem with all his heart and with all his soul, there is no repentance greater than this." "<b>However,</b> according to what I explained in parashat Ki Tavo (Deuteronomy 28:15), both regarding the matter of the blessings and regarding the matter of the curses, that there are three general categories in the commandments of HaShem: the first is the engagement of Torah; the second, observance of negative commandments; the third, fulfillment of positive commandments —" "<b>Therefore,</b> when it came to state the rectification of repentance, it arranged all three of them. Corresponding to repentance for Torah study, it stated the first repentance: ״וְשַׁבְתָּ עַד ה׳״, and concluded ״וְשָׁמַעְתָּ בְּקוֹלוֹ״, which is Torah study, and it mentioned nothing else alongside it — and this is the beginning of repentance that the penitent must do. And corresponding to it He said ״וְשָׁב ה׳ אֶת שְׁבוּתְךָ וְשָׁב וְקִבֶּצְךָ״ etc., as they said, of blessed memory (Zohar vol. III 72a), that in the merit of engagement in Torah Israel will be redeemed. He also said ״עַל מָה אָבְדָה הָאָרֶץ״ etc., ״וַיֹּאמֶר ה׳ עַל עָזְבָם אֶת תּוֹרָתִי״ (Jeremiah 9:11–12); therefore, when they return to Torah study, HaShem will gather them and bring them into the land that they inherited, etc." "<b>And corresponding to</b> the observance of negative commandments, it said ״וּמָל ה׳ אֱלֹהֶיךָ אֶת לְבָבְךָ״ etc. For it is known that the foreskin of the heart is the doing of evil and the love of evil, since a person's heart is his coveted thing. Corresponding to this it said ״וּמָל״ etc. ״לְאַהֲבָה אֶת ה׳״ — meaning, that you clothe the love which was implanted within you when He fashioned you in creation, in the pleasantness of the intimacy of the affection of your Elohim. And He designated a reward for this: that HaShem will turn all the troubles away from us upon our enemies, as He said ״וְנָתַן״ etc. ״עַל אוֹיְבֶיךָ״ etc." "<b>And corresponding to</b> the fulfillment of positive commandments, it said ״וְאַתָּה תָשׁוּב״ etc. ״וְעָשִׂיתָ אֶת כָּל מִצְוֹתָיו״ — here are positive commandments. And He designated for them the reward of bestowing benefit, as He said ״וְהוֹתִירְךָ״ etc., and He will again rejoice, etc."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:20:32.912158660Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}